{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/402942-werewolf-inspiration","id":402942,"title":"Werewolf inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-11T21:10:43-08:00","id":402942,"title":"Werewolf inspiration","content":"Stupid question. I still can't wrap my head around how to make werewolves distinct. I think this is partly due to the book over-emphasizing the common wolfyness of all Uratha, and partly due to my general unfamiliarity with werewolves, perhaps. I can't see a way to play up the animalistic and rage-filled aspects of their character sufficiently while avoiding turning them into caricatures and/or making them all way too similar. <br /> <br /> I get the pack dynamic fairly and have plenty of fictional and non-fictional sources to look to for examples there. Same for the Shadow.<br /> <br /> My problem is that I can't think of any media to look to that portray werewolves similar enough to the Uratha to be useful, the problem being that most werewolf stories are about solitary and, more importantly, uncontrolled lycanthropes. The only possible exception to this I can think of is Teen Wolf, which i admit, I haven't seen yet. I also thought perhaps Being Human might work but (A) it's still basically the story of one werewolf, and he's still at least somewhat cursed and (B( I watched a couple of episodes of the American version and it kinda soured me on the whole franchise (especially since i know they used the same plots.)<br /> <br /> Any other suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:23:17-08:00","id":403023,"title":"","content":"Teen wolf is ok for it in a spirit cop sort of way. The book recommends cop dramas, which works for the characters... but perhaps maybe something like Jack Nickleson in &quot;wolf&quot;, Mr. Jones as a film is a good example of the kind of shit you deal with in the Hisil. American werewolf in london and ginger snaps are both good films for first change wolves dealing with rage frenzy. What about &quot;Wolves&quot; which just went for sale on the playstation store? Fairly good violent film, featuring inter uratha violence. <br /> <br /> For books you could read something like Anne Rice wolf gift, while not really being similar to the Uratha has inter pack play and a sort of world building you may be looking for. Dog soldiers is a pretty good example of pack workings, all be it more of a hunter film example. American Werewolf in Paris has this whole werewolf cult thing going on. <br /> <br /> The Uratha, as they appear to be in 2nd edition, are more in line with the horror stories of the past, while still keeping the game themes as they were. What might help you with the Uratha is the Rage (players guide) Lore of the forsaken (good for cultural stuffs but not really necessary at all) and hunting grounds the rockies. It gives a clear example of Uratha activities within their respective regions. Tribes of the moon and The Pure will cement what each particular tribe of werewolves mean/how they act, though you can supplement the former with &quot;the Rage&quot;. <br /> <br /> Not sure if this helped any... you'll be hard pressed to find films that show werewolves as the Uratha are... you can find films and activities similar to what the Uratha do, but not enough with werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:27:44-08:00","id":403029,"title":"","content":"That's kinda my problem. I have enough examples of werewolves going off the rails, as that's a common trope of the genre. There aren't nearly enough examples of werewolves NOT acting like mindless rage machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:36:43-08:00","id":403043,"title":"","content":"and my hesiitation when it comes to looking at books to figure it out is that I'm reluctant to spend money on a game I don't &quot;get&quot; especially when it could just be that werwolves aren't my thing and I have to accept that. Besides I do much better with narrative when it comes to grasping the &quot;feel&quot; of a game. I have looked at some actual plays, which often works well, but the characters still felt far too similar, possibly because all the games I looked at were first change games, and possibly because I just don't like werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:42:55-08:00","id":403047,"title":"","content":"That could all be a thing. Have you checked outr the Manitou springs demo? Its free and comes with sample characters, and details their progression throughout the storyline. Honestly the werewolves do not have to be mindless rage beasts, thats just with the low harmony. For the most part they're fairly functioning folk. I get that not wanting to spend money part too, otherwise I'd buy demon the descent (not sure where I sit on that one either, quick start looked pretty rad). Perhaps it's more that the players themselves are making overly similar characters trying to play werewolf archetypes. Perhaps try this... make a character as a character. Their own personality and stats and what not, then add the werewolf template to them. Give them their own life, within the bounds of being a werewolf. Something that embraces being a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T00:00:13-08:00","id":403086,"title":"","content":"if you're looking for Demon inspiration I suggest Donnie Darko, and paying attention to the angels in Supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:00:05-08:00","id":403359,"title":"","content":"Werewolves have fundamentally human emotions, albeit with greater than life passions. They don't have crushes, theirs is love at first sight. They don't get offended, they will plot how they'll kill you and make it look like a suicide, or coerce you to take your own life at their own terms. They don't have protegees, they have cubs, which will be protected with fang and talon.<br /> <br /> The way those emotions are magnified by their spiritual passions informs how they approach their lives as several hunts. Seeking out one's loved one, despite the fact that you're a forsaken creature with alien entities that would love nothing than to wear your sweetheart like a sock puppet would keep any Uratha up at night, making sure the Spirit World isn't restless. The process of having someone take their own life, after coercing him to make amends for their slight and set their matters in order would be arduous and completely ethical for most Bone Shadows. And finally, mentoring the next generation of Uratha, passing down the traditions that have lasted for millenia is ingrained in their very being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:06:26-08:00","id":403364,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have werewolves, but Sons of Anarchy is still a great source for Werewolf; specifically the themes of taking on responsibility, personal growth and the sacrifice that comes with it. There's also the pack, the rage, the idea of territory, the concept of using the tools of the barbarian to help ordinary people (and in doing so, alienating oneself irrevocably from ordinary people), fatherhood and the responsibility thereof, etc. Plus lots and lots of barely concealed anger and violence. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:02:59-08:00","id":403419,"title":"","content":"I suggest the Graphic Novel Welcome to Hoxford by Ben Templesmith. Its a good portrayal of a pack of werewolves with pack structure and hunting being central to their culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:36:08-08:00","id":403436,"title":"","content":"Is that by chance available on kindle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T10:50:17-08:00","id":403486,"title":"","content":"It is but as the separate issues. It came out as a four issue mini-series and then was collected later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T11:18:22-08:00","id":403502,"title":"","content":"This is for first edition. You might want to wait until second edition comes out before you decide to get anything.<br /> <br /> An important thing to remember is that they aren't rage-filled people until they've hit some Death Rage triggers, are nearing their auspice moon, or are using their gauru form. Your average werewolves aren't Bruce Banner, going to turn into a rampaging hulk because someone made fun of their hair. That's just the more easily angered people to begin with, or werewolves who are low on harmony. Primal Urge did it too, bringing a large penalty to any social rolls.<br /> <br /> You're free to play them as people with anger issues, but that's just a narrow facet of Uratha as a whole. When it comes down to it, aside from what Ephsy has already mentioned, they're normal if usually passionate people. But some are going to be cool and collected, some are going to be temperamental hot heads, some are going to be nearly disassociative in their interactions, and some just don't care. The signature characters in the core book range from a descendant of railroad barons who runs his protectorate like he runs his international corporation, a confident woman from a family that own a lot of defense contractors for the US Military, a guy from the suburbs trying to finish their psychology degree, to a biker with a heart who doesn't like drunk drivers on his road, the veteran who loves to let loose, and an old bigot who's a patriarch of his clan.<br /> <br /> I think the Shield is a good example of werewolves. Vic Mackey's Strike Force are cops, the rest of the department may as well be a Protectorate. Mackey has a skewed view of things but when it comes to crime he's more about control than elimination. Getting rid of drug dealers will just cause more trouble down the road as other forces move to fill the vacuum left in their absence, so let some dealers do their work, and feel free to take a little off the top. Even the gangs could be compared to packs. The problem with this is it ends to focus on very street level kind of things, which is good, but as we've discussed elsewhere can lead people to thinking all werewolves are bikers and gangbangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T13:39:28-08:00","id":403646,"title":"","content":"What I find most interesting is how none of us has suggested the idigam fiction anthology on sale at drive thru for something like 2$. That would be your best example of how the uratha act in given situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T13:42:53-08:00","id":403648,"title":"","content":"alokov said they didn't want to spend money. But that would be a good route. There was also the wolf book in the Three Shades of Night book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T15:30:57-08:00","id":403751,"title":"","content":"That gangster stereotype is kinda the root of my problem. Don't get me wrong I'm a major organized crime buff, and the main impetus behind my desire to understand werewolf was reading a book on the Hell's Angels (so Sons of Anarchy was already on my list <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but I need a broader understanding than that to avoid making all my werewolf characters slight fariations on Joe Pesci or Tony Soprano. There are a couple of examples I can think of that sort of break that stereotype while still being gangsters (Nucky Thompson and Jimmy Darmitty from Boardwalk Empire) Nucky is much more calm and Jimmy is a good example of the calm calculated, long-term revenge that somebody mentioned.<br /> <br /> Trying to stretch my brain a bit, would you say that Captain Picard could be an Elodoth Alpha? He certainly gets angry when somebody like Q messes with him but he never comes off as somebody with a real temper problem. Playing off that, Malcolm Reynolds, especially the whole &quot;you're part of my crew&quot; thing could work. And, again, you have the forces of barbarism as the good guys, sort of. <br /> <br /> Not quite there yet, but I think I've zeroed in on the problem (getting caught in a pit of stereotype) so that should make it easier to fix. <br /> <br /> The reason I thought I might just not like Werewolf in general is that I tend to vasty prefer characters that live by their wits and charm (i e Mental and Social primary) to more physical ones. I'm aware, of course that there are auspices and tribes based around not being physical, but, again, given my limited grasp of the setting, and the few examples I had seen of it in play, which all emphasized the rage and the stereotypes, it was hard to see past that issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T15:48:21-08:00","id":403786,"title":"","content":"Really, any show that focuses on a tightly-knit group would help for pack dynamics. Leverage, for instance. Picard, the crew from Firefly, all of them.<br /> <br /> I can appreciate why you'd think werewolves have to be more physically aspected, but the truth is they can go any way, especially since the various forms can boost their physical Attributes to average or higher numbers when they don't normally have them, and their gauru form in second edition is going to be a monstrous combatant for anyone. But fighting is just a part of what werewolves do. Patrolling territory and spotting out claimed and ridden and dealing with spirits can rely a lot on mental and social abilities. There's Lodges, groups of werewolves that have the same outlook or goals, that are solely made of police officers, scientists, and doctors. Many of the sample Fire-Touched are very charismatic religious people, and I've already mentioned some of the signature characters that are more high class business people. While werewolves are going to expect packmates to likely be able to defend themselves at least a little, the hunt is a group effort, and even if one packmate isn't a ferocious fighter they're still helping, whether through harrying the target or other ways.<br /> <br /> Black Sails might be a good show to watch, too. While there is fighting, there's plenty of cunning and wisdom thrown around too. It's easy to sort of see each crew as a pack, some of which fall apart by the end of the first season. And there's plenty of characters who rely solely on their wits and charm, like Jack Rackham, Max and John Silver, who have shown very little in the way of physical abilities but still manage to be interesting major characters via their charm and wits. There's even a few characters like the Guthrie woman who lack physical ability and social charm and have to rely entirely on wisdom and resources. Them being pirates can seem like them just being 'aquatic gangbangers' but they're not all like that.<br /> <br /> As an added benefit, when push comes to shove so many of the characters have shown themselves capable of great savagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T16:22:56-08:00","id":403836,"title":"","content":"what I'm getting from this is that most of the stories I look to for Hunter could work equallly well for Werewolf. In that case, I still probably won't play Werwolf too often, cause most of the time I'd probably rather do Hunter, but I still love the spirit world, and I love the pack dynamic, so I'm sure I'll use werewolf at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T16:46:30-08:00","id":403851,"title":"","content":"Yes, there's a lot of overlap there. Keeping the worlds separate and dealing with those who muddy the lines, and protecting your own and killing the monsters that prey on them.<br /> <br /> With the mythical background, however, you kind of get more to do than just kill. A lot of things hunters would just try and kill, werewolves may be willing to negotiate with. Not that hunters don't negotiate, but with spirits and other things it can often be the only way to go for a werewolf. And while their can be Bale Hounds and other things tearing packs apart from the inside, the Pure aren't really comparable to the hunter cancer cells outside of maybe Division Six. The Pure werewolves want the world to become like it was, Pangaea, so they can take their place as lords of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:31:04-08:00","id":404011,"title":"","content":"Congratulations, you have sold me a book. I will definitely be picking up Forsaken 2nd edition when it comes out, and if I like I'll add it to the game lines I follow (along with Mage and Hunter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:48:03-08:00","id":404019,"title":"","content":"Cool, I hope you like them, from what we've seen 2nd edition is a big step forward from first, adding more to the tribes while also having some more freeform systems like with rituals. A big thing will be incorporating wolf-blooded and humans into packs. They may not know exactly what's going on, but whether they're wrangled into your gang, neighborhood watch or corporate board room, they're part of a larger team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}